<article id="entry-hades-leh" class="entry-card" data-dictionary="grego" data-source="LEH" hidden><header class="entry-header"><div><h1 class="entry-title greek">ᾅδης</h1><div class="entry-meta"><span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="ᾅδης, -ου · hadēs" data-transliteration="hadēs" data-meanings="Hades|mundo inferior|inferno|sepultura|morte">ᾅδης, -ου</span><span class="separator">·</span><span>substantivo masculino da 1ª declinação (N1M)</span><span class="separator">·</span><span>frequência LEH: 7-4-20-43-37=111</span><span class="separator">·</span><span>também usado no NT (+)</span></div></div><div class="source-tag">LEH</div></header><div class="entry-divider"></div><section class="entry-section"><div class="section-title">Tradução literal</div><p class="entry-text"><strong>Hades, mundo inferior, inferno</strong> (<a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.37.35" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gn 37.35</a>); <strong>sepultura</strong> (<a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/3MA.4.8" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">3Mc 4.8</a>); <strong>morte</strong> (<a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/WIS.1.14" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sb 1.14</a>).</p>
<p class="entry-text"><span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="εἰς ᾅδου · eis hadou" data-transliteration="eis hadou" data-meanings="ao Hades">εἰς ᾅδου</span> (<span class="abbr-help tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="abbr" data-tooltip-label="sc." data-tooltip-text="scilicet — isto é; a saber">sc.</span> <span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="οἶκον · oikon" data-transliteration="oikon" data-meanings="casa">οἶκον</span> ou <span class="greek greek-term tooltip-trigger" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="greek" data-tooltip-label="δόμον · domon" data-transliteration="domon" data-meanings="casa|morada">δόμον</span>): <strong>ao Hades</strong> (<a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.42.38" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gn 42.38</a>).</p>
<p class="entry-text">Na maioria das vezes, equivale ao hebraico <bdi class="hebrew hebrew-token tooltip-trigger" lang="he" dir="rtl" tabindex="0" data-tooltip-type="hebrew" data-tooltip-label="שׁאול" data-transliteration="šʾwl" data-meanings="Sheol|mundo inferior">שׁאול</bdi>, <strong>Sheol, mundo inferior</strong>.</p>
<p class="entry-text"><strong>Ocorrências citadas inicialmente:</strong> Gn 37.35; Gn 42.38; <a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/GEN.44.29" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">44.29</a>,31; <a class="reference reference-link" href="https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/LXX/NUM.16.30" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nm 16.30</a>.</p>
<p class="entry-text"><strong>Cf.</strong> LARCHER 1983, 204-205 (Sb 1.14); VAN HOONACKER 1905, 398-399; → NIDNTT; TWNT.</p></section></article>
